\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Effective rank $\ensuremath  {r_{\mathrm  {eff}}}\xspace  (H)$ vs.\ penultimate dimension $d$ on log-log axes, averaged across tasks per architecture. All three pools show $\ensuremath  {r_{\mathrm  {eff}}}\xspace  $ growing monotonically with $d$ (positive Spearman $\rho $ reported in legend), empirically confirming Lemma\nobreakspace  {}\ref {lem:mp} ($\ensuremath  {r_{\mathrm  {eff}}}\xspace  = \Theta (d)$). Dashed/dotted lines have slope\nobreakspace  {}$1$ (reference for linear scaling); the two lines reflect different $c(\gamma ) = e^{C(\gamma )}$ constants across architecture families and pooling regimes. VTAB uses $n{=}1000$ subsampled features, placing large-$d$ architectures in the $n < d$ regime where $\ensuremath  {r_{\mathrm  {eff}}}\xspace  \leq n$, hence the lower VTAB band.\relax }}{13}{figure.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:reff_d}{{3}{13}{Effective rank $\reff (H)$ vs.\ penultimate dimension $d$ on log-log axes, averaged across tasks per architecture. All three pools show $\reff $ growing monotonically with $d$ (positive Spearman $\rho $ reported in legend), empirically confirming Lemma~\ref {lem:mp} ($\reff = \Theta (d)$). Dashed/dotted lines have slope~$1$ (reference for linear scaling); the two lines reflect different $c(\gamma ) = e^{C(\gamma )}$ constants across architecture families and pooling regimes. VTAB uses $n{=}1000$ subsampled features, placing large-$d$ architectures in the $n < d$ regime where $\reff \leq n$, hence the lower VTAB band.\relax }{figure.caption.14}{}}
